WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:04.450
Hey there, how are you doing today?

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:07.849
In this class, we'll leave glass and translucent effects

3
00:00:07.849 --> 00:00:10.730
to the side, and we'll learn about something completely

4
00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:12.140
new.

5
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:15.980
We'll be introducing a brand new shading model,

6
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.370
and that is the two-sided foliage,

7
00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:24.329
which is used to texture foliage like trees or grass.

8
00:00:24.329 --> 00:00:26.250
This one is going to be pretty interesting,

9
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.739
so let's get started.

10
00:00:28.739 --> 00:00:30.980
Two-sided foliage is a particular one

11
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:34.280
because it really focuses on giving to our vegetation

12
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.380
a realistic and consistent feel when it's hit by the light.

13
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.219
Now, whenever we talk about the specifics of a shader

14
00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:44.219
when hit by a light, we really

15
00:00:44.219 --> 00:00:47.020
start referring to the subsurface scattering

16
00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.460
of a material, which is also typically

17
00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.979
responsible to create the effect of our skin

18
00:00:52.979 --> 00:00:55.179
when it's close to the light.

19
00:00:55.179 --> 00:00:57.520
They know when it gets actually redder,

20
00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.619
that's subsurface scattering.

21
00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.060
The two-sided foliage shading model

22
00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:05.299
enables us to customize the subsurface scattering

23
00:01:05.299 --> 00:01:10.260
of a surface and set how light transmission is simulated.

24
00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.099
We need to be careful, though, because when using Nomen,

25
00:01:13.099 --> 00:01:16.140
there are a couple of things we need to take care of first.

26
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.180
We need to first make sure that the mobility

27
00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.780
setting of our vegetation is set to movable,

28
00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.859
and therefore contributing to our dynamic lighting.

29
00:01:24.859 --> 00:01:26.739
And also, we'll have another checkbox

30
00:01:26.739 --> 00:01:28.659
to take care of in the Details panel,

31
00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:31.540
where we'll need to make sure Evaluate World Position

32
00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.700
Offset is enabled as well.

33
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:36.620
But I'll show you in just a second how to do that.

34
00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:39.519
Now, as usual, I'll be jumping directly into the engine

35
00:01:39.519 --> 00:01:40.739
and close the slides.

36
00:01:40.739 --> 00:01:44.620
But remember that each step that I will be taking in Unreal

37
00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:48.180
will also be displayed through screenshots and instructions

38
00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:51.180
here in the PowerPoint file that is at your disposal,

